---
intent: >
  installAgents spec names a stale six-agent roster with old role names
  (aide-researcher, old aide-domain-expert) and inverted model assignments,
  contradicting the canonical Pipeline Agents table in .aide/docs/index.md
  which defines eight agents with the current names and model tiers.
misalignment:
  - spec-gap
---

## Issues

- [x] `src/tools/init/installAgents/.aide` outcomes.desired[0]: "Six agent files are installed: aide-spec-writer, aide-researcher, aide-domain-expert, aide-architect, aide-implementor, aide-qa"
  The canonical Pipeline Agents table (.aide/docs/index.md) defines eight agents. Two are missing from this spec: aide-aligner and aide-auditor. The spec also uses stale names: "aide-researcher" no longer exists (renamed to aide-domain-expert), and the old "aide-domain-expert" was renamed to aide-strategist.
  Traces to: .aide/docs/index.md -> Pipeline Agents table (eight agents, current names)
  Misalignment: spec-gap

- [x] `src/tools/init/installAgents/.aide` outcomes.desired[4]: "opus for deep reasoning (spec-writer, domain-expert, architect), sonnet for throughput (researcher, implementor, QA)"
  The canonical table assigns: opus to spec-writer, strategist, architect, aligner, auditor; sonnet to domain-expert, implementor, QA. The spec has domain-expert on opus (should be sonnet) and researcher on sonnet (agent no longer exists; domain-expert is the research agent and is sonnet). The model assignment description is inverted for the renamed roles.
  Traces to: .aide/docs/index.md -> Pipeline Agents table (model column)
  Misalignment: spec-gap

- [x] `src/tools/init/installAgents/.aide` outcomes.desired[2]: "Obsidian MCP is declared for agents that need brain access -- researcher (write), domain-expert (read), architect (read)"
  The canonical table shows brain access for: domain-expert (write), strategist (read), architect (read + playbook), auditor (read + playbook). The spec uses stale names and omits auditor entirely.
  Traces to: .aide/docs/index.md -> Pipeline Agents table (Brain Access column)
  Misalignment: spec-gap

- [x] `src/tools/init/installAgents/.aide` intent paragraph: "spec-writer, researcher, domain-expert, architect, implementor, QA"
  Lists six roles with stale names. Should list eight roles with current names: spec-writer, domain-expert, strategist, architect, implementor, QA, aligner, auditor.
  Traces to: .aide/docs/index.md -> Pipeline Agents table
  Misalignment: spec-gap

- [x] `src/tools/init/installAgents/.aide` Strategy section: "Seven agents map to the seven distinct roles"
  The canonical pipeline has eight agents. The strategy also describes "researcher and domain expert" as separate agents, but these are now "domain-expert" (research phase) and "strategist" (synthesize phase).
  Traces to: .aide/docs/index.md -> Pipeline Agents table (eight rows)
  Misalignment: spec-gap

- [x] `src/tools/init/installAgents/.aide` Context section: "seven phases (spec, research, synthesize, plan, build, QA/fix, refactor)"
  The canonical pipeline includes the align phase. Eight phases total, not seven.
  Traces to: .aide/docs/index.md -> Pipeline Agents table (align phase present)
  Misalignment: spec-gap

## Retro

The agent rename (aide-researcher -> aide-domain-expert, aide-domain-expert -> aide-strategist) and the addition of aide-aligner and aide-auditor updated the canonical docs (.aide/docs/index.md), the actual agent files (.claude/agents/aide/), and the initContent registry (src/tools/init/initContent/index.ts), but did not propagate to the installAgents spec. An alignment check should have been run after any commit that changes the Pipeline Agents table, since every init submodule spec encodes facts from that table. The spec-writer should have called aide_discover and cross-referenced the canonical table before writing outcomes that enumerate agents by name and count.
